course: dictionary
lesson: 10283
title: Torpor: sleepy and slow
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words describe a feeling and also a science fact. Torpor is one of them. Read the words around it to find out which meaning fits. «The heat filled us with torpor.» Heat makes you slow, heavy and sleepy, so torpor here means a lazy, sleepy feeling with no energy.
explain: Science texts use the same word in a different way. «Hummingbirds save energy at night in a deep sleep called torpor.» The words called and save energy are your clues. In animals, torpor is a short sleep-like state where body temperature and heartbeat drop to save energy.
explain: Look for clues that show the meaning. «Echidnas can survive bushfires by hiding in burrows or logs and lowering their body temperature and heartbeat, a state called torpor.» The word state and the words lowering their body temperature tell you torpor is a special kind of slow, low-energy state.
explain: Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it. If torpor means a sleepy, slow state, does «The heat filled us with a sleepy, slow state» still make sense? Yes, so you have it right.
fact: Torpor means being very sleepy, slow and inactive, without energy.
fact: In animals, torpor is a short sleep-like state when body temperature and heartbeat drop to save energy.
fact: «Hummingbirds» and «bats» and some «mice» can go into torpor, often at night.
fact: Long-lasting torpor in winter is called hibernation.
fact: Torpor is uncountable: you say «a state of torpor», not «a torpor».
exercise: «The heat filled us with torpor.» What does torpor mean here? | A cold drink | A loud noise from the heat | *A heavy, sleepy, slow feeling | Bright, busy energy
exercise: «Hummingbirds save energy at night in a deep sleep called torpor.» What is torpor in this sentence? | Flying very fast | *A sleep-like state where body temperature and heartbeat drop | Eating lots of nectar | Dancing in the air
exercise: Which clue in «Echidnas ... lowering their body temperature and heartbeat, a state called torpor» helps you work out what torpor is? | Hiding in burrows | Bushfires | Their body temperature is about 32 degrees | *Lowering their body temperature and heartbeat
test: Mia says torpor means being wide awake and full of energy. Is she right? | Yes, it means very loud | *No, it means sleepy and slow, without energy | Yes, it means full of energy | No, it means a kind of food
test: The lesson says long-lasting torpor in winter has a special name. What is it? | Migration | *Hibernation | Camouflage | Summer torpor
exam: Which word is closest in meaning to torpor? | *Lethargy | Speed | Excitement | Noise
